            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 828)</h2>
<ul>
<li>Side-by-side and stacked movie exports size their cells by the same even-pixel rule as every other export, so a picture of odd width no longer wears a hairline of letterbox in the pair export that the single-clip export doesn&#8217;t have.</li>
<li>Web review: on a hosted share the picture read about a fifth darker than the proxy on every Mac &#8212; the page&#8217;s &#8220;Auto&#8221; gamma, meant for the browser&#8217;s video lift, was also applied to the live-trim canvas, which has no such lift. The canvas now shows the proxy&#8217;s own values; an explicit gamma preset still applies everywhere.</li>
<li>On a phone, the web review&#8217;s toolbar no longer scrolls: two rows upright &#8212; transport, then Draw, Color, Playlist and Full screen &#8212; and one row sideways.</li>
<li>Manual figures reshot: the EXR frames were darker than the app shows them (a figure-script setting, not the app), and the web figures carry the fixes above.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
