h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 823)</h2>
<ul>
<li>Stills show as recorded. A PNG, JPEG or TIFF was being de-gamma'd twice on the way in and then tone-mapped by the ACES view, so a dark picture went nearly black on screen and in every grab and export (sRGB 40 read 0, 128 read 35). A still now carries its own code values, like a movie frame, and its default input space is the display-referred <b>Output - sRGB</b> &#8212; through the sRGB view a still round-trips within a level, and the color check suggests the same space.</li>
<li>If you had set a still to <b>Linear sRGB</b> or <b>sRGB - Texture</b> to compensate, set it back &#8212; Color &#9656; input space, or the color check&#8217;s suggestion.</li>
<li>Optimized stand-ins made from PNG/JPEG/TIFF sequences by earlier builds held the old values and now count as stale; optimize them again.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
